# "Spend this mana only to cast an Angel spell" (CR 106.6): on turn 3 Giada is Bot1's only source of mana (the Black Lotus paid for her on turn
# 1) and her {W} is the only mana in its pool, so `! Bot1.Hand.Hinterland Sanctifier.Cast` - a one-mana white creature spell, which that white
# mana would pay for if it could - is not offered. The positive control is the same mana in the same pool paying for an Inspiring Overseer
# (an Angel) once the Moxen are cast for the rest of its cost. The Overseer enters with Giada's counter, a 3/2.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Giada, Font of Hope
Hinterland Sanctifier
Mox Pearl
Mox Jet
Mox Ruby
Inspiring Overseer
Island x14

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Giada, Font of Hope.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: White)
Bot1.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Giada, Font of Hope.Activate
? Bot1.Mana = {W} (AngelSpells)
! Bot1.Hand.Hinterland Sanctifier.Cast(Mana: short)
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Inspiring Overseer.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Pass

[Expect]
Stack.Count = 0
Bot1.Battlefield.Inspiring Overseer.Power = 3
Bot1.Hand = Hinterland Sanctifier; Mox Ruby; Island; Island
